From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: orangepi5: drop sd-uhs-sdr104 (SD card reliability)

SDR104 at 150 MHz is the fastest, most signal-marginal UHS-I mode and
is a suspected cause of intermittent SD card corruption. Drop it; the
slot falls back to high-speed (50 MHz, 3.3 V). Shared dtsi, so this
also covers the Orange Pi 5 variants that include it.

NOTE: precautionary, not yet proven to fix the corruption (could not be
reproduced on a known-good card). Validated only that the card drops
SDR104 -> high-speed 50 MHz.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
index 9da13f9..038ad7b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dtsi
@@ -473,7 +473,6 @@
 	max-frequency = <150000000>;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vcc_3v3_sd_s0>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vccio_sd_s0>;
 	status = "okay";
-- 
